# Machine-readable twin of "Betrieb & Migration" in v1.18.0.md (Issue #709). The release notes and
# scripts/release-rehearsal.sh walk THIS list, in this order; a change to the steps in the notes
# changes this file in the same commit.
#
# Format:  phase | expected exit | id | kind | argument
#   expected exit: one code or a comma list; audits exit 2 when they list findings, which is information, not a failure
#   phase   pre = before the deploy (read-only), migrate = prisma migrate deploy, post = after it
#   kind    sql = psql -c on the throwaway DB, script = `pnpm tsx scripts/<arg>` in the new api image,
#           migrate = `prisma migrate deploy` as the image entrypoint runs it
# Operational steps with no exit code to prove (pg_dump, MINIO_* on every stage, the demo compose
# update) stay in the notes only.
#
# Notes "Betrieb & Migration": Personen ohne Rollenzuweisung (#641, nur Information)
pre|0|role-gap-sql-641|sql|select count(*) from "User" u join "Employee" e on e."userId"=u.id where u."isActive" and not (e."firstName" = U&'Gel\00F6scht' and e."lastName" like U&'GEL\00D6SCHT-%') and not exists (select 1 from "RoleAssignment" ra where ra."userId"=u.id and ra."tenantId"=e."tenantId");
# Deploy: the migration of #641 (drop User.role and the enum Role; one-way, pg_dump first)
migrate|0|migrate-deploy|migrate|
